# Optional: let onn-rgb's daemon read hotkeys from the onn keyboard's input
# event nodes. By default the daemon grabs the Fn node (event5) and re-emits
# its keys minus Fn via uinput (see 72-onn-uinput.rules); the main node
# (event4) is grabbed only with block-combo-keys. Only needed for
# `onn-rgb daemon` hotkeys and `onn-rgb listen-keys`.
#
# systemd/elogind distros: TAG+="uaccess" gives the user at the local seat
# access (file must sort before 73-seat-late.rules, hence "71-").
# Non-systemd distros without elogind: uaccess does nothing; instead add your
# user to the `input` group (`sudo usermod -aG input $USER`, then log out/in).
# Note: either way, that user can read every key typed on this keyboard.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3938", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1296", MODE="0660", GROUP="input", TAG+="uaccess"
